(Plan 230 stage A4 — version 0.1 of `parts`. Linked with parts_1_0.vox into one
.so so a consumer can `see` BOTH versions from one `.lib` and call a function
present in only one of them. `common` is exported by both versions (so a call to
it would be ambiguous — the dual case); `only one` is exported by 1.0 only, so
a consumer importing both versions and calling `only one` resolves to exactly
one provider and neither errors nor warns. That is the per-name resolution
guarantee: ambiguity is a property of the called name's provider set, not of
the import set, so a non-ambiguous name in a multi-version import just works.

`hasflag` is not used here; `common` returns n add 1 in this version.)

Library parts version "0.1".

To common with a number called n.
  Return a number, n add 1.